prompt:
You are assisting with business process modelling. List the steps of the business process described below.

INSTRUCTIONS
- A step is one thing that an actor does in the process. Use only what the description states. Do not add steps that the description does not state.
- Give every step: step_id (S1, S2, ... in the order of the description), actor (who does it), activity (what is done, in a few words), data_or_object (the data, document or object the step handles; empty string if none) and quote.
- quote: copy the words of the description that state the step, word for word. Do not change, shorten in the middle or rephrase the words.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE (made up, for the format only)
Description: "The customer chooses a product. The shop sends the product and an invoice."
Answer: {"steps": [{"step_id": "S1", "actor": "customer", "activity": "choose a product", "data_or_object": "product", "quote": "The customer chooses a product"}, {"step_id": "S2", "actor": "shop", "activity": "send the product and an invoice", "data_or_object": "product, invoice", "quote": "The shop sends the product and an invoice"}]}

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "Step": {
      "properties": {
        "step_id": {
          "description": "S1, S2, ... in the order of the description",
          "title": "Step Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "actor": {
          "description": "Who does the step",
          "title": "Actor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "activity": {
          "description": "What is done, in a few words",
          "title": "Activity",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "data_or_object": {
          "description": "The data, document or object the step handles; empty string if none",
          "title": "Data Or Object",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "quote": {
          "description": "Exact words copied from the process description that state the step",
          "title": "Quote",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "step_id",
        "actor",
        "activity",
        "data_or_object",
        "quote"
      ],
      "title": "Step",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "steps": {
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/Step"
      },
      "title": "Steps",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "steps"
  ],
  "title": "StepsOutput",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
An e-commerce company has a comprehensive order fulfillment process:
When a customer places an order, the system records the order details.
Payment processing begins.
If the payment fails, the customer is notified, and the process ends.
Upon successful payment, the inventory system checks stock availability.
If items are out of stock, a back-order is initiated, and the customer is informed about the delay.
The process continues once the back-order is received and all required items are available in stock.
In-stock items are picked from the warehouse.
Quality control checks are performed on the picked items.
Packaging is done, including gift wrapping if the customer requested it.
Meanwhile, the shipping department prepares shipping documents and labels.
If the order is international, customs documentation is prepared.
Once packaging and shipping documents are ready, the order is dispatched.
The system sends a shipping confirmation to the customer.
After dispatch, the system updates the inventory levels.
A follow-up email for feedback is sent directly after confirming the successful delivery.
If the customer reports any issues upon delivery, a returns process is initiated, which includes:
Sending a return shipping label.
Receiving returned items.
Inspecting returned items.
Processing a refund or replacement.
The customers are private persons in several EU countries. Some customers contact the company a few days after delivery only because they no longer want the items, without reporting any issue.
